          "notes": "Design gate already produced an Approved decision record + fully-written reports.md v0.20 spec section for this story; implemented per that spec exactly. Backend: added get_monthly_pnl_by_tax_year (database.py) and an optional year param on get_monthly_pnl_report()/GET /reports/monthly-pnl (backward-compatible; omitting year is unchanged rolling-window behaviour). Frontend: TaxYearReport's notice link now passes its selectedYear up to Reports' new monthlyInitialYear state; MonthlyPnlTable gained its own Tax Year filter (Select, same pattern as the Tax Year tab's own selector) seeded from that value, defaulting to the current UK tax year on direct tab navigation (reset via the plain nav button's onClick). Opportunistic in-file fixes (small, same-file, disclosed in commit): corrected reports_endpoints.md's stale 'No query parameters' line to also document the pre-existing, previously-undocumented format=csv param; reordered the CSV download URL to format=csv&year=... so an existing test's exact-prefix route regex still matches; added a wildcard to one pre-existing test's exact-string monthly-pnl route mock in reports-performance-tab.spec.js (broken by the new always-present ?year= query string). Also fixed a real, already-committed regression from this same session's ST-01 partial-migration batch pass: Reports.js's Tax Year Trades Table pnl_pct cell had been incorrectly given the three-way zero-neutral colour rule during ST-01's opportunistic zero-P&L fixes -- DEV-REPORTS-ST01-02/decision_record.md §5 explicitly scopes that convention to the Realised P&L column only; reverted to the original two-way rule (>0 emerald / else rose), confirmed by tests/e2e/reports-realised-pnl-zero-colour-convention.spec.js SC-RPZ-05 (which was failing before this fix, passing after). New tests: tests/test_monthly_pnl_tax_year_filter.py (6 backend unit/endpoint tests, all passing) and tests/e2e/tax-year-restated-notice-year-scoped-link.spec.js (3 Playwright scenarios covering the story's own 'older tax year' AC, direct-navigation default, and re-filter behaviour -- all passing). Full backend suite (1861 tests) and the full existing Reports/Monthly/TaxYear Playwright suite re-run clean after all fixes. Two genuinely pre-existing, unrelated test issues discovered during this regression pass were NOT fixed in-line (out of this story's scope) -- one already tracked (BLG-QA-190, test_monthly_ai_cost.py's unrestored sys.modules['database'] swap, confirmed via git-stash bisection to reproduce identically pre-ST-03), one newly filed (BLG-QA-197, reports-performance-tab.spec.js SC-REP-04a's stale zero-P&L sign-convention assertion, also confirmed pre-existing via the same bisection method)."
